---

!! Syntax

```
wardley-beta
    title [Map title]
    anchor CustomerName [visibility, evolution]
    component ComponentName [visibility, evolution] (build|buy|outsource)
    ComponentA -> ComponentB
    ComponentB -> ComponentC
    evolve ComponentName target_evolution
```

''Axes:'' Y-axis is visibility (0 = invisible to customer, 1 = highly visible); X-axis is evolution (0 = Genesis/novel, 1 = Commodity/utility). Positions are written `[visibility, evolution]` — Y first, X second (counter-intuitive).

|!Keyword|!Description|
|`anchor`|Customer or user node (shown as diamond)|
|`component`|Technology or service component with position and optional decorator|
|`(build)`|Build-vs-buy strategy decorator|
|`(buy)`|Purchase/license strategy decorator|
|`(outsource)`|Outsource strategy decorator|
|`->`|Dependency link (value flows from left component to right)|
|`+>`|Flow/value link (alternative arrow style)|
|`evolve`|Planned evolution arrow to target evolution position|
|`note "Text" [y, x]`|Floating annotation on the canvas|

!! Tips

* Position coordinates are `[visibility, evolution]` — Y-axis first. This is counter-intuitive: `[0.9, 0.1]` means highly visible (top) but still in genesis (left).
* `anchor` nodes represent customers or users; `component` nodes represent capabilities and technology.
* `evolve ComponentName 0.8` adds an arrow showing planned movement along the evolution axis.
* Wardley Maps do not use color-by-category; components are distinguished by their position and strategy decorator.
* Links must be written pairwise — one `A -> B` per line. Chained links (`A -> B -> C`) are ''not'' supported by the `wardley-beta` parser and cause a syntax error; split each hop onto its own line.
* `wardley-beta` is still beta — complex layouts may not render exactly as expected.

